 "headline": "Champi passed within 12 miles of Guam's southern tip on 18 October with its core of extreme winds mostly offshore, then became a super typhoon over the Philippine Sea and on 21 October tied Sinlaku (April) for the highest winds of 2026 worldwide: 185 mph (1-minute). Taiwan's weather agency expects it to turn north off Taiwan's east coast rather than make landfall, bringing extremely heavy rain to Taiwan through 24 October, then rain to eastern China, the Ryukyus, South Korea and southern Japan before it dissipates over Japan around 26 October.",
